From f518c3aec38057e0a9954e2de1ef74b0332f3f85 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 22:48:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kanban): partition sync-thread local and Board CPU
 [daveey]

The first post-deployment P1 could not resolve the unchanged local <=1%
acceptance: sync.board includes synchronous Board HTTP and JSON CPU. The
saved 1.98% inclusive result therefore proved neither local success nor
failure. A scope amendment authorized bounded accounting and one new P1,
not a threshold waiver or further performance/harness experiments.

Measure completed same-thread loop iterations and nested board services;
exclude only outermost Hub._call CPU, including serialization, HTTP/TLS,
retries, fallback and decoding. Keep wait_for_work CPU and attachment
caller preparation conservative/local. Preserve existing inclusive passes.
Separate-thread attachment transfers, feed and metrics work are explicitly
outside this envelope, never subtracted from calling-thread CPU. Document
completed-service and equal-run snapshot requirements.

Proof: decorator-omission RED gives 4 failures; restored 82 tests across
partition/timing suites and 74 loop-accounting/metrics consumers pass.
Full scripts/check --base origin/main passes. Full affected consumer gate
runs separately before publication. No new live P1 or runtime change.
